### Expected behaviour

When timer pools are exhausted, SGW-C should gracefully reject or drop excessive Create Session Requests (optionally respond with an appropriate GTP-C error cause such as "No resources available"/"System failure"), handle allocation failures without triggering assertions, continue running to preserve service continuity.

### Observed Behaviour

Under repeated Create Session Requests, SGW-C hits:
ogs_pool_alloc() failed in ogs-timer.c, and then
a fatal assertion xact->tm_peer in ogs_gtp_xact_remote_create (xact.c:219),
causing open5gs-sgwcd to abort and dump core, resulting in Denial of Service (DoS).

### eNodeB/gNodeB

No

### UE Models and versions

No

