### Expected behaviour

When the bearer pool is exhausted, SGW-C should not crash. Instead it should:
detect allocation failure (bearer == NULL),
return an appropriate GTPv2-C error (e.g., reject session/bearer establishment due to resource exhaustion),
and keep the process running (log a warning/error).

### Observed Behaviour

When ogs_pool_id_calloc fails due to bearer pool exhaustion, sgwc_bearer_add asserts on a NULL pointer (ogs_assert(bearer)), causing immediate process abort.

